{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "ambient-tape — three tapepad layers and a dusty beat, at 61bpm in A.",
    "",
    "tapepad is a polyphonic pad played through a tape machine: a stack of",
    "detuned oscillators per note, then one shared transport (wow and flutter",
    "bending the whole chord together) and one shared tape stage (saturation,",
    "bit crush, bandwidth limit, hiss). Three of them here, all reading the",
    "ambientchords pack:",
    "",
    "  pad     slow-bloom     the chords, mid register, 10-bit",
    "  haze    halo           a slower, wider, dirtier layer an octave up",
    "  drone   drone-fifths   open fifths dropped an octave, sub wide open",
    "  drums   dusty          hiphopdrums, through a tape saturator",
    "  verb    reverb bus; echo  dotted-eighth delay bus",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /pad wow=60 8b             warp the tape, slowly",
    "  /pad wow_rate=3 8b         and make the warp faster",
    "  /pad bits=5                cheap sampler; 12 and up is clean",
    "  /pad sat=6 4b              drive the tape harder (louder, too)",
    "  /pad cutoff=400 16b        close it right down — the sub stays",
    "  /haze hiss=0.6             tape noise as an instrument",
    "  /pad voices=5 detune=30    thicker, and further out of tune",
    "  /chords variation=0.7      revoice the progression",
    "  /chords pattern=tidal      a different one from the same pack",
    "  /harmony root=53           move it all to F",
    "  /drums stop                just the pads",
    "",
    "Two LFOs, showing both kinds of patch into a synth param:",
    "",
    "  sweep -> pad.cutoff    read once per note, so each chord enters at a",
    "                         different brightness rather than sweeping mid-note",
    "  wobble -> haze.wow     a real AudioParam, so it moves continuously and",
    "                         the top layer drifts in and out of stability",
    "",
    "wow and flutter are one transport shared by every note, not one per voice",
    "— a tape machine has one capstan, and that is why the chord bends together",
    "instead of smearing into a chorus.",
    "",
    "master runs a goodenizer called 'glue' — compressor, saturator, tilt EQ",
    "and limiter in one box. /glue shows how hard it's working, /glue mix=0",
    "takes it off."
  ],
